{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fec640df-85aa-489c-b61a-597c991f7812","agentId":"afd5fd0b447a75fb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (FastAPI cuore/; mes lib only via cuore/services/*_bridge.py). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, no Edge, minimal grepping. Report under 100 words. Plan: docs/research/SYSTEMS_DIVE_IN_PLAN_2026-10-08.md, Phase 2 only. Another agent is editing cuore/web/templates/systems.html, systems_bridge.py and creating system_detail_bridge.py/system_routes.py/system.html: you may add at most ONE line to systems.html (a <script src=\"{{ static_url('systems_map.js') }}\" defer> tag at the end) and ONE line to the map template to add data-system=\"<key>\" on each cell if missing (check first; if cells already carry an id \"sys-<key>\" use that and change nothing). Do not touch any other existing file except cuore/app.py (or wherever api routers are included) to register your API.\n\nBuild: (1) cuore/api/systems_map.py: GET /api/systems/{vin}/state -> per system key: state (ACTIVE / CLEARED_UNVERIFIED / STALE / NO_DATA / VERIFIED_CLEAN using the existing verdict/dossier helpers, grep -l \"CLEARED_UNVERIFIED\" cuore/services once), open_code_count, codes; edges: list of {a, b, lift, sessions_together, confidence, source, kind} from systems_bridge.correlate(vin) and the dependency table; sessions: ordered list of {id, when, systems_fired[]} from the car's scan history (reuse whatever correlate() uses). Read-only. (2) cuore/web/static/systems_map.js + systems_map.css (link the css from the js by injecting a <link>, so systems.html needs only the script line): on load fetch the state, colour each cell by state (red active, amber cleared-unverified, grey stale, dim no data, green verified clean; use existing CSS variables from cuore.css, e.g. --sev-*, --ok), add an open-code count badge, draw hot edges thick with the lift value between cells that fired together (SVG overlay positioned from getBoundingClientRect, recomputed on resize), wording \"seen together on this car\" in the tooltip, never \"depends on\"; a legend; a session time slider under the map (range input, 48px thumb, labels with the session date) that highlights the cells fired in that session and dims the rest, with a \"Now\" position restoring the live state. Works at 710px, no horizontal scroll, nothing under 12px. (3) cuore/tests/check_systems_map_api.py (CUORE_STATE_DIR temp dir before import, TestClient): endpoint 200 with 25 keys, every state in the allowed set, edges have lift and sessions_together, no edge text contains \"depends on\", unknown VIN gives an empty-but-valid shape. Run it and check_screens.py."},"uuid":"46150eee-65e8-466b-a4b2-59344af684ee","timestamp":"2026-10-08T20:20:16.556Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
