lean signal exists yet), applied only when a system's own codes are all CLEARED_UNVERIFIED — a reasonable approximation given current data, worth flagging if a future phase adds per-system readiness confirmation."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":167793,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SD6yAuKoCu64pAPhbYTNA4":{"message":"Phase 2 built and verified.\n\nNew files:\n- cuore/services/systems_map_bridge.py — system_states() (5-state vocabulary via dossier_bridge/mes_bridge, same pattern as system_detail_bridge), edges() (co_occurrence ∪ dependency table, no \"why\" text), sessions() (rebuilt from mes.analysis.dtc_history + mes.systems.systems_for_code, same inputs correlate() uses internally).\n- cuore/api/systems_map.py — GET /api/systems/{vin}/state, read-only.\n- cuore/web/static/systems_map.js / systems_map.css — paints cells by state, open-code badge, SVG hot-edge overlay (thick, lift label, \"seen together on this car\", resize-safe), legend, 48px-thumb session slider with \"Now\" reset. CSS uses existing --sev-*/--ok tokens, responsive at 710px, min 12px text.\n- cuore/tests/check_systems_map_api.py — 16/16 passing.\n\nTouched existing files (minimal, as scoped):\n- cuore/app.py: added systems_map import + app.include_router(systems_map_api.router, prefix=\"/api\") (merged around the other agent's concurrent edits, re-diffed before applying).\n- cuore/web/templates/systems.html: one line, `<script src=\"{{ static_url('systems_map.js') }}\" defer>`.\n- cuore/web/systems_svg.py (the actual map-drawing module, not systems_bridge.py/systems.html which the other agent owns): one line adding `data-system=\"{key}\"` to each cell's `<a>` — cells had no prior id/data attribute, so nothing was skipped.\n\nVerified: check_systems_map_api.py (16/16) and check_screens.py (28/28) both pass; systems page renders 200 with script tag + data-system present, no template errors.\n\nNote: VERIFIED_CLEAN is derived from the whole-car dossier verdict (no per-system monitor-confirmed-clean signal exists yet), applied only when a system's own codes are all CLEARED_UNVERIFIED — a reasonable approximation given current data, worth flagging if a future phase adds per-system readiness confirmation."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3f4ac0c4-372a-4212-8906-e8ec29b93b02","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfqRR5GzdXD2q5bwhCjfZ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ce96b86-bf38-44da-bf60-4c7420f3ae13","timestamp":"2026-10-08T20:44:18.523Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
